<div class="text-center">
	<h2>
		The Drivers
	</h2>
	<p>
		Racing drivers are the gladiators of the modern age. The comparison to a
		gladiator describes taking part in the Dakar very aptly. Despite high safety standards,
		almost every year a driver is killed. Most often it is the less protected
		motorcycle riders, but car and truck pilots are not immune to fatal accidents
		either. Here we pay the tribute they deserve to the brave men and women who fought
		their way through the sands of North Africa in a Pajero.
	</p>
